  "limitations": [
    "Current acceptance used short real CPU fixtures and guided dialogue, not hour-long GPU research, distributed checkpointing or native popup interaction.",
    "Plan observation passed within one actual read-only host turn. Plan-only does not itself schedule another turn; model/tool latency is not strict real-time monitoring.",
    "First-step timing and cooperative save receipts require trainer integration. Caller-supplied timing alone cannot attest actual first-step execution.",
    "Hardware sampling is not atomic reservation; explicit device restrictions, resource ceilings, scheduler allocations, review gates and interruption permission still apply.",
    "Existing frozen production owners and external scheduler deadlines are not hot-patched by installation. The previously blocked production Goal was not resumed by this repair.",
    "All native cases retain their own source snapshots; the final queue wording and release-CI correction are covered by the ordinary case/package reruns rather than claiming every case used identical metadata.",
    "The original local Python 3.14.7 run retained its publication-list failure; the targeted correction and subsequent complete native CI, including the exact release commit, passed. Overlapping test counts are not additive.",
    "The exact release commit passed complete Linux/macOS and both native Windows shell gates before publication. The official public archive was downloaded, verified and installed; the follow-up main commit records publication metadata only."
  ],
